  "full_text": "They talk about the luck of the Irish, right? And what does that mean? You know, I used to kind of groan about, oh no, is that some kind of fairy shit or something? Oh no, some kind of leprechaun fairy shit. And then like, just now I kind of came up with a rabbi explanation. So like, you know there's perfect justice. Today's meditation is on, like if you... If you give a cigarette to somebody, you should get something for it. Because it's righteousness. And you're really not supposed to create work for God. Because now God has to go settle the balances, right? Because now God has to go work out to do justice. Because you just gave something for free. Anyway, so the Irish are kind of, I think the word is meek. Yeah, I think that's the right word. I'm trying to get precise vocabulary. They don't stick up for themselves, right? So, like, and they're also kind of, you know, God said he's angry with creationists for bringing shame with their stupidity. The view, what they're doing is they're kind of like, they're too meek. Well, actually, that's not it. God corrected my, I thought it was meekness, you know, like, oh, no, whoever. Whoever got fired for buying IBM, right? I thought it was meekness. I thought it was like the creationists were really meek. Dude, grow some balls, man. But God said it was they're stupid. So anyway, if you're meek, then you don't stick up for yourself. And if you're Irish, you probably... you play it safe and give more than you have to you know like oh i don't know i don't know like uh what's uh imagine alfalfa or somebody like uh like something happens right he like panics and like uh and like uh overcompensates right so so the irish are getting like a bank account of of overpayments right at least the ones that are lucky right so where would this come from right and uh anyway so the meek will inherit the earth",
